<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Czech Silesia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Czech Silesia is the part of the historical region of Silesia that lies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opava">Opava</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrava">Ostrava</a>. It descends from the small part of Silesia that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> kept after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> conquered most of the region in 1742, ruled as Austrian Silesia until 1918. In 1928 it was merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravian-silesian-land">Moravian-Silesian Land</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/czech-silesia.jpg" alt="Czech Silesia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michal Klajban · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kamenit%C3%BD_(Moravskoslezsk%C3%A9_Beskydy).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
